<https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/HSE-ERM-ControlOntology#FirstLineOfDefence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/HSE-ERM-ControlOntology#Control> .
<https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/HSE-ERM-ControlOntology#FirstLineOfDefence> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2024-05-15"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/HSE-ERM-ControlOntology#FirstLineOfDefence> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "Nick McDonald" .
<https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/HSE-ERM-ControlOntology#FirstLineOfDefence> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://www2.healthservice.hse.ie/organisation/national-pppgs/hse-integrated-risk-management-policy/> .
<https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/HSE-ERM-ControlOntology#FirstLineOfDefence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/HSE-ERM-ControlOntology#> .
<https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/HSE-ERM-ControlOntology#FirstLineOfDefence> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "the way risks are managed and controlled day-to-day. Assurance comes directly from those responsible for delivering specific objectives or processes. Its value comes from those who know the business, culture and day-to-day challenges."@en .
<https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/HSE-ERM-ControlOntology#FirstLineOfDefence> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "First line of defence"@en .
